From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valix <djvalic.wc@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] reactor: drop a completion's waiter when pause() raises

ReactorCompletion.wait() added the current greenlet to the waiting list
and removed it only after pause() returned. When pause() raised (pauses
disabled, as in a klippy:ready handler; SAVE_VARIABLE waits on the
threaded executor), the greenlet stayed in the list, and the later
complete() called update_timer() on its None timer: AttributeError
'NoneType' object has no attribute 'timer_is_running' in the reactor,
which used up klippy's one retry for unhandled exceptions. Kiln OS: remove
it in a finally. The ReactorError still reaches the caller.
---
 klippy/reactor.py | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/klippy/reactor.py b/klippy/reactor.py
index 3ba351b..a43ca43 100644
--- a/klippy/reactor.py
+++ b/klippy/reactor.py
@@ -35,8 +35,13 @@ class ReactorCompletion:
         if self.result is self.sentinel:
             wait = greenlet.getcurrent()
             self.waiting.append(wait)
-            self.reactor.pause(waketime)
-            self.waiting.remove(wait)
+            # Kiln OS: also when pause() raises (pauses disabled, as in a
+            # klippy:ready handler): a greenlet left in the list made the
+            # later complete() call update_timer(None, ...)
+            try:
+                self.reactor.pause(waketime)
+            finally:
+                self.waiting.remove(wait)
             if self.result is self.sentinel:
                 return waketime_result
         return self.result
